<title>UK: Unibank sets $200 million 10-year step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>Unibank sets $200 million 10-year step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   UNIBANK</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	BASE	*3M-LIBOR  MATURITY	 MAY.07</p>
<p> TYPE STEP-UP FRN     MARGIN    *+40 BP    PAY DATE    28.MAY.97</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A3	  ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   55.5 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *FOR FIRST SEVEN YEARS THEN STEPS UP TO 3M LIBOR</p>
<p>		+190 BP.</p>
<p>	    **CALLABLE FROM YEAR SEVEN AT PAR.</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 50	  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  DENMARK   TAX PROVS   GROSS UP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    30 BP     SELL CONC  25.5 BP   PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
